# Testing Standards

## Test Pyramid

```
        /\
       /  \      E2E (few)
      /----\     - @SpringBootTest + TestRestTemplate
     /      \    - Full HTTP flows, critical paths only
    /--------\   Integration (some)
   /          \  - @DataJpaTest for repositories
  /------------\ - @WebMvcTest for controllers
 /              \
/----------------\ Unit (many)
                   - Model classes (entities, value objects)
                   - Service logic (with mocked repos)
```

## Test Location

Tests follow the same package structure as main code:

```
src/test/java/com/duoc/LearningPlatform/
├── controller/
│   └── OrderControllerTest.java     # @WebMvcTest
├── service/
│   └── OrderServiceTest.java        # Unit test
├── repository/
│   └── OrderRepositoryTest.java     # @DataJpaTest
└── model/
    └── OrderTest.java               # Unit test
```

---

## FIRST Principles

- **Fast**: Tests must run quickly
- **Isolated**: Each test is independent, no shared state
- **Repeatable**: Same result every time
- **Self-validating**: Clear pass/fail
- **Timely**: Written at the right time (before code in TDD)

---

## Naming

- Names in English
- Represent business rules, not implementation details
- Use domain language

```java
class OrderTest {

    @Test
    void confirmsOrderWithItems() { }

    @Test
    void rejectsConfirmationOfEmptyOrder() { }

    @Test
    void doesNotAllowAddingItemsToConfirmedOrder() { }
}
```

## AAA Structure (Arrange-Act-Assert)

- **Arrange**: Prepare context and data
- **Act**: Execute the action
- **Assert**: Verify the result
- Visually separate the three sections with blank lines

---

## Unit Tests (Model + Service)

### Model Tests — No Spring, no mocks

```java
class OrderTest {

    @Test
    void confirmsOrderWithItems() {
        Order order = new Order("Ana");
        order.addItem(new OrderItem(someProduct(), 2));

        order.confirm();

        assertEquals(OrderStatus.CONFIRMED, order.getStatus());
    }

    @Test
    void rejectsConfirmationOfEmptyOrder() {
        Order order = new Order("Ana");

        assertThrows(IllegalStateException.class, order::confirm);
    }
}
```

### Service Tests — Mock repositories with Mockito

```java
import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class OrderServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Mock
    private ProductRepository productRepository;

    @InjectMocks
    private OrderService orderService;

    @Test
    void createsOrderSuccessfully() {
        Product product = new Product("Widget", 10.0);
        when(productRepository.findById(1L)).thenReturn(Optional.of(product));
        when(orderRepository.save(any(Order.class))).thenAnswer(i -> i.getArgument(0));

        Order result = orderService.createOrder("Ana", 1L, 3);

        assertNotNull(result);
        verify(orderRepository).save(any(Order.class));
    }

    @Test
    void throwsWhenProductNotFound() {
        when(productRepository.findById(99L)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());

        assertThrows(ResourceNotFoundException.class,
                () -> orderService.createOrder("Ana", 99L, 1));
    }
}
```

